## IP & CIDR
10.0.0.0/16
4 octects having CIDR of range 16


10. - 00001010
0. -  00000000
0. -  00000000
0. -  00000000
Out of 32 bits, 16 bits are usabel IP space.
First 2 octets or 17 bits locked & last 2 octets are in unlocked bits & allows full range of possible IP's
2^16 = 65,536 IPs can be used for Host part


AWS VPC's can use CIDR ranges betweeen /16 & /28

/16 - 65536
/17 - 32768
/18 - 16384
/19 - 8192
/20 - 4096
/21 - 2048
/22 - 1024
/23 - 512
/24 - 256
/25 - 128
/26 - 64
/27 - 32
/28 - 16


In Every subnet the 1st fours & last 1 IP address are reserved for AWS use.

> Public Subnet - Includes a routing table entry to an **Internet Gateway** to support inbound .outbound access to the Internet.

> Private Subnet -  Do **NOT** have routing table entry to an Internet Gateway & are **NOT** directly accessible from the public Internet

> Typically use a Jump box (NAT/proxy/Bastion host) to support restricted, **outbound only** public Internet access.